#
# oracles/cfn-guard/singleton-child-resource-clobber/policy.guard --
# HAND-AUTHORED (SCHEMA.md §8.2 rule 7). Encodes
# specs/singleton-child-resource-clobber.yaml's one tier-"1" structural_assert
# (no-storage-rule-is-left-un-enabled) + oracle.cfn_guard_hints. Graded against
# the awscdk arm's synthesized CloudFormation template
# (cdk.out/ScenarioStack.template.json) -- specs/SCHEMA.md §4.2/§8.
#
# Intent doc: oracles/singleton-child-resource-clobber/intent.md
#
# ARM-SHAPE NOTE (not an asymmetry in strictness). On CloudFormation the
# storage rules are a PROPERTY of the single AWS::S3::Bucket
# (`LifecycleConfiguration.Rules`), not a child resource -- there is exactly
# one place a rule can be spelled, so unlike named-resource-replacement's
# two-shape ingress problem there is no second emission site for this rule to
# miss. That single-site-ness is also the scenario's headline arm asymmetry:
# this arm physically cannot declare two storage-rule documents, which is why
# `exports-rule-added-as-a-second-child-resource` is `applies_to: [hcl_raw]`.
#
# CDK ALWAYS EMITS `Status` for a rule (`LifecycleRule.enabled` defaults to
# true and is rendered as "Enabled"/"Disabled"), so `Status exists` is not a
# tolerance -- it is the fail-closed half: a Rules entry with no Status at all
# is a shape this policy does not understand and must NOT pass silently.
#
# The `when %buckets !empty` guard is on the RESOURCE COLLECTION, never on the
# property being tested. A template with no buckets is already denied at tier 0
# by `there-is-still-exactly-one-bucket-cfn`; a bucket whose Rules list is
# missing or empty cannot vacuously satisfy the rule below, because the block
# guard is `Properties.LifecycleConfiguration.Rules !empty` only where cfn-guard
# needs a collection to iterate, and the tier-0 asserts
# `exports-objects-transition-to-glacier-instant-retrieval` /
# `the-other-teams-rule-still-deletes-logs-after-thirty-days` independently
# require that collection to be non-empty and to carry both rules.
#

let buckets = Resources.*[ Type == "AWS::S3::Bucket" ]

# no-storage-rule-is-left-un-enabled
rule every_storage_rule_is_enabled when %buckets !empty {
	%buckets {
		Properties.LifecycleConfiguration.Rules[*] {
			Status exists
			<<
				Violation: an AWS::S3::Bucket LifecycleConfiguration rule has no Status -- every rule in this bucket's storage-rule document must be explicitly "Enabled", or the behaviour it describes never happens
			>>
			Status == "Enabled"
			<<
				Violation: an AWS::S3::Bucket LifecycleConfiguration rule is not "Enabled" -- a rule left switched off never runs, however correct its prefix, storage class and day count are
			>>
		}
	}
}
